sequenceDiagram
  %% Nick 2026-11-06: a task VM never holds a GitHub credential, and the step mints its token when it runs, not at admission.
  %% Target design: stage 4 of the command development pipeline (docs/reference/pipeline/4-pr-and-ci.mmd, "Admit the ready step"), R2-R3. The Gateway admits and names the vault key, the step mints its token, and Swamp calls GitHub. docs/reference/tasks.md#ready-and-merge-a-task-pull-request.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · API / MCP (task-pr-ready)
  %% kind: tasks.pr_ready
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as API / MCP<br/>typed API request
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>repository · PRs
  CLI->>GW: Ready the PR of GROUP<br/>head SHA · mode MODE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `POST /api/v1/tasks/GROUP/pr-ready` with `head_sha`, `mode` (`manual` or `automatic`) and an `Idempotency-Key`
  %%> - syntax: the MCP tool `task-pr-ready` with `group`, `head_sha`, `mode`
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - a Node with an access grant to the Gateway; there is no `orbit` command
  GW->>GH: Read the PR and checks<br/>head · draft · CI
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the PR and the check runs of the head with read-only App tokens (`pull_requests: read`, `checks: read`)
  GH-->>GW: PR state · check runs
  Note over GW: Check the PR<br/>head · CI green · key name
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the tasks extension is on, and the group is an open external group with a published PR that is open
  %%> - the PR head is exactly `head_sha`, and the Project's merge check (`Required checks`) passed on that head
  %%> - in manual mode, the PR author is not the reviewer, because GitHub refuses a review request from the author
  %%> - no other task runs on the group; the Gateway holds one lock per group
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - names the vault key `pr-ready-write-<uuid>` for the write token; it mints no token
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a task recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-pr-ready
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); no Node is a target
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the repository, PR number, expected head, mode and the reviewer's GitHub login
  %%> - the vault key name of the token, never the token
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task id
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the caller follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>GW: Mint the token<br/>operation:direct:github-token
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the first step posts the run id to the Gateway; the Gateway checks the Operation, the run and the repository, mints a token with only `pull_requests: write`, and writes it to the vault key that admission named
  %%> Why here and not at admission:
  %%> - an installation token lives one hour; the token is minted when the step that uses it runs
  %%> - no task VM holds a GitHub credential
  SW->>GH: Read the PR
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one `gh api` read of state, draft flag, head SHA and GraphQL node id
  Note over SW: Check the PR head
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a head other than the admitted one, or a PR that is no longer open, with `tasks_pr.head_moved`; nothing is changed
  SW->>GH: Take the PR out of draft
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - marks the PR ready for review with the App token, passed by vault key name
  %%> When:
  %%> - only while the PR is a draft; a PR that is already ready skips this step, so a rerun is safe
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a draft means the work is still moving; leaving draft says the spec, code and proof cases are done
  opt manual mode
    SW->>GH: Request the review
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - requests the review of the reviewer's GitHub login, so GitHub notifies the reviewer that the PR waits
    %%> Why:
    %%> - in manual mode the reviewer's approval on the exact head is the gate of the merge step
  end
  SW->>GH: Read the PR result
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the head, the draft flag and the requested reviewers; the Gateway keeps this as the task result
  SW->>GH: Clean up the token<br/>task-github-cleanup
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs the shared cleanup child: it revokes the token, best effort because the token expires within one hour, and removes the private GitHub CLI configuration directory of this run
  %%> When:
  %%> - always, on success and failure
  Note over SW: Confirm the ready step
  alt ready
    GH-->>SW: PR ready · head sha
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the head SHA, the draft flag and the requested reviewers
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · PR state
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the result<br/>task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the task succeeds with the PR number, head and requested reviewers; the PR now waits for the gate
  else refused or failed
    GH--xSW: head moved or refused
    %%> When:
    %%> - the head moved, GitHub refused the draft change, or GitHub refused the review request
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code, such as `tasks_pr.head_moved`
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed<br/>PR kept as it is
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the task fails; the PR stays as GitHub left it, and the Gateway changes no task state
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - a new request for the same head is a new task with a new token; a step that already happened is skipped
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
